codex
One practical knob is the hard `8192` sample cap. On public synthetic runs at width 64, the current candidate leaves FLOP headroom below the 0.1 multiplier floor, while at width 128 it can already sit above the floor. I’m testing whether a conservative adaptive cap beats the fixed cap on generated data.
